{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1780873575,"nonce":"jiQZ/P+Xl0L8HooM/d1hVfVv7w8=","metadata":{"github-id":"UCE_lAHOK4fCvM8AAAABEd6MVM7CR-J2"},"target":"0f2da64872ef3047996702c553850a0af036341f4322c64d96d33a633772716c","message":"## Purpose\n\nNext on-water deployment — **pre-class shakedown** (before the June 8 class start / dev\nfreeze), de-risking the June survey. The headline new item: the **CA safety node**\n(`ca_safety_node`) is now the **default helm gate** on BizzyBoat (replacing the nav2\nCollision Monitor), so this deployment's primary goal is to **validate it on water**.\nCarries over the unfinished #205 goals (clean survey lines, sensor/sonar readiness, OTH).\n\nMerged just before this deployment: rolker/unh_marine_navigation#64 (node),\nrolker/seafloor_echoboat_project11#43 + this repo #227 (wiring + 240 overlay).\n\n## Update (2026-06-07) — ran, analyzed, and going into production\n\nDeployed twice on **2026-06-05** (two test runs; the run-B bag is ~99 min on water). Full\npost-hoc bag analysis is in the [analysis comment](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/228#issuecomment-4644280232)\nbelow and `~/data/logs/analysis/2026-06-07_issue228/`.\n\n**This is the last controlled shakedown before the boat goes into production** (Summer Hydro\nclass → Lake Massabesic survey). From here the remaining validation items are answered by\n**harvesting the bags that production survey / teaching runs generate**, not by dedicated tests\n— see the roadmap restructure (#233 / PR #235).\n\n- **Goal 1 (CA gate):** mechanism **validated on water** — exact idle passthrough, yaw-preserving\n  slowdown (52/56 episodes), reverse-assisted stop (clamped −0.5 m/s), yaw cancelled during\n  reverse (350/350 samples). **Gaps:** no clean *high-speed autonomous* obstacle pass\n  (interventions ≤~1.5 m/s); sole-publisher not fully graph-confirmed (no double-publish WARN).\n  New issue: **rolker/unh_marine_navigation#73** — CA gate chatters STOP during autonomous hover.\n- **Goal 3 (yaw accel):** **RESOLVED — not a regression.** ±3.0 is the deliberate field tune\n  (±0.5 was too slow → line-following hunting), test-locked in seafloor#45; both YAML and test\n  agree at 3.0. Residual watch: snap-roll ≤~22° on sharp autonomous yaw reversals (sub-deployment-197).\n- **Goal 2 (carry-forwards):** now **harvest from production** — a clean survey-line set, the\n  turning-limit check, sensor / QINSy readiness, and OTH all come from real survey / teaching\n  runs. The action item is **recording the right topics** (no re-run once in production).\n\n## Goal 1 — Validate the CA safety helm gate (primary)\n\nThe node replaces the Collision Monitor with a **speed-scaled, yaw-preserving slowdown +\nreverse-assisted stop** — the fix for the #205 near-miss/\"stops dead in front of the\nobstacle and can't turn off it\" deadlock. Validate:\n\n- [ ] **Pre-water gate (sim):** run the **yaw-sign-in-reverse** sim test. Until it passes,\n      `cancel_yaw_during_reverse` stays **true** (straight reverse brake) — do **not** enable\n      the yaw-passthrough path on water this deployment.\n- [x] **Nominal survey unchanged** — no obstacle ⇒ cmd_vel passes through; speed/yaw same as before.\n- [x] **Slowdown behaves** — boat slows earlier/proportionally to speed as an obstacle enters\n      the forward corridor, **while still able to turn** (the anti-deadlock mechanism); the\n      avoider gets room to steer clear.\n- [x] **Reverse-assisted stop** — in the stop box the boat brakes to a stop (reverse thrust),\n      bounded by the distance/duration backstop (stern is unsensed — confirm it doesn't run\n      aft past the cap; the duration backstop is the odom-independent bound).\n- [ ] **CAMP viz** — yellow (slowdown, **sized live by speed**) + red (stop) boxes render and\n      **fill** on activation (driven by `CollisionMonitorState`); ties into #183.\n- [ ] **Sole helm publisher** — Collision Monitor is gone from the chain; the node logs a\n      warning if it ever sees \u003e1 publisher on the helm topic. Confirm no double-publish.\n- [ ] **Fallback drilled** — `use_ca_safety:=false` reverts to the Collision Monitor; confirm\n      the one-line field revert works before relying on the new gate.\n\nRelated/after: reverse-*arc* escape + rotate-in-place is the principled follow-on\n(rolker/seafloor_echoboat_project11#42); recovery-BT back-off is rolker/unh_marine_navigation#67.\n\n## Goal 2 — Carry-forwards from #205\n\n- [ ] **A clean survey-line set** under control (never cleanly delivered through #173/#186/#201/#205).\n- [ ] **Avoider + chart inflation (rolker/unh_marine_navigation#63)** — the #205 swerving was\n      root-caused to the avoider weaving along the pier's 150 m chart-layer inflation gradient.\n      Re-test the AvoidanceController deviation now that the safety gate changed underneath it.\n- [ ] **Sensor/sonar readiness** for student software integration — M3 pings + 1PPS + QINSy\n      export, SBG nav, AML SVS; survey-data recording pipeline captured end-to-end.\n- [ ] **OTH re-test** (#130) — Starlink-only completed survey line at range.\n- [ ] **Offload QINSy data** (carry-over from #205).\n\n## Goal 3 — Verify the pre-existing yaw-accel finding\n\n- [x] **velocity_smoother yaw accel/decel** — `nav2_params.240.yaml` currently has\n      `max_accel`/`max_decel` z = **3.0 / -3.0**, but the #36 governor intent (and\n      `test_param_compose`) is **0.5 / -0.5**. Confirm on water whether this is a real\n      governor regression (6× intended yaw accel) or a stale test, and fix/triage. (Surfaced\n      during the #43 review; not yet triaged.)\n\n## Success criteria\n\nCA safety gate validated on water (slowdown + reverse-stop behaving, no deadlock, viz +\nsole-publisher confirmed, fallback drilled) with the yaw-passthrough path left off pending\nthe sim test; a clean survey-line set recorded with valid M3/SBG/SVS data; one OTH line.\nLogs at `docs/logs/2026/2026-MM-DD_\u003chost\u003e_logs.md` per the per-deployment convention.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":5,"timestamp":1780640917,"nonce":"9Zr6rYWLjXIK8bJBttjfAq6RxzY=","metadata":{"github-id":"LE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABEd6MVM8AAAAGI-Qmbw"},"added":["deployment"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"timestamp":1780642896,"nonce":"g/QyWeWn8d3o/xVMZfVbittZBtw=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABE-lERQ","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/228#issuecomment-4629021765"},"message":"## Carry-forward: M3 multibeam patch test (confirm mount orientation/offsets)\n\nThe M3 → CAMP live-coverage pipeline is now built and merged end-to-end:\n`kongsberg_em_bridge` (rolker/marine_tools#14) → `detections_to_pointcloud` →\n`cube_bathymetry_node` → `GridMap` (CAMP auto-renders). The `bizzy/m3` URDF frame\n(#222) and the perception-launch wiring + config (#226) are in. Validated offline\nagainst the 2026-06-04 recovery bag — coherent ellipsoid coverage, valid per-ping\nTPU.\n\n**What still needs the water: a patch test.** Two things are *nominal* and want\nfield confirmation:\n\n- **Orientation / handedness.** The driver's angle convention is fixed from the\n  Kongsberg spec (beam pointing +port, tx tilt +fwd → SonarDetections +stbd/+fwd),\n  so the patch test validates the **URDF mount**, not a driver sign. The\n  `base_link → bizzy/m3` transform is `rpy=(π,0,0)` (normally-mounted downward).\n- **Mounting offsets.** `x=-0.23, y=0.0, z=-0.145` are `[MEAS] rough` from the #77\n  install log.\n\n**Procedure:** run the M3 over a discrete feature (the cod rock works) with\nreciprocal and crossing lines at a couple of speeds, watch CAMP coverage / compare\noverlapping swaths. Roll error → depth tilt across-track; pitch error → fore/aft\noffset of the feature between reciprocal lines; yaw error → feature smears\nlaterally with heading. Feed corrections back into the `bizzy/m3` transform in the\nURDF (rolker/unh_echoboats_project11#221 / #77), not the driver.\n\nRefs: marine_tools#14, #221/#222, #226, rolker/cube_bathymetry#31, #77.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1780644603,"nonce":"gMHJ9MK5Q/LecaVIxlSCFZPWh40=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABE-wSfQ","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/228#issuecomment-4629205629"},"message":"### Add to Goal 2 — line-following controller upgrade to tune on the water (nav#66)\n\nMerged since this issue was written: the **CrabbingPathFollower upgrade**\n([`rolker/unh_marine_navigation#72`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_navigation/pull/72),\ncloses #71; the top-priority nav#66 line-following work). It directly serves the \"clean\nsurvey-line set\" goal above. **All new behaviour is behind params that default to today's\nbehaviour and are live-tunable via `ros2 param set`** (same workflow as the perception layer),\nso this is opt-in tuning on the water.\n\nAlways-on (no tuning needed — bug fixes):\n- [ ] **Progress-preserving localization** — confirm the cross-track reference no longer\n      *snaps backward* during a weave (the 5–9 m `pid_state.error` step that fed the loops/360s).\n- [ ] **Bounded backward re-localization** — confirm same-goal path reshapes don't leave the\n      follower aiming from a stale segment.\n\nTo tune (opt-in, on a clean survey line):\n- [ ] **Pure-pursuit look-ahead** — set `FollowPath.lookahead_time` (~3 s to start; `L = V·T`)\n      and confirm the boat anticipates bends / stops over-correcting. With look-ahead on, retune\n      the cross-track PID toward **I-only** (look-ahead distance becomes the cross-track-tightness\n      dial; I keeps the current crab).\n- [ ] **Inner-loop gain / clamp** — tune `FollowPath.heading_rate_gain` and\n      `FollowPath.max_yaw_rate` (the yaw command is now a tunable, clamped heading-error loop;\n      the velocity_smoother still enforces the physical rate/accel limits underneath).\n\nNotes:\n- This pairs with the existing **nav#63** re-test item (avoider weaving) — both feed the clean-line goal.\n- The CAMP path/marker **viz recolor** ([`rolker/unh_marine_navigation#70`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_navigation/pull/70), open)\n  reserves red/green for the plan's editable/locked state — worth merging before this deployment\n  so the path overlays are legible while tuning.\n- Ties into Goal 3 (velocity_smoother yaw-accel 3.0 vs 0.5 intent) — that clamp is what the inner\n  loop relies on; resolve alongside.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1780670885,"nonce":"sXULhEKkW0D+kgN3MQTlDUQV5RM=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABFCLI1w","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/228#issuecomment-4632791255"},"message":"## Carry-forward: test the Garmin GCV sidescan driver on-water\n\nNew driver `garmin_sidescan` (rolker/marine_tools#15, PR\nhttps://github.com/rolker/marine_tools/pull/17) is ready for its first live\nvalidation — the one thing captured-data tests can't cover. The GCV-20\ntransducer is being installed on BizzyBoat now. This deployment is a good\nopportunity to exercise it (low-risk: it's passive imagery + a safety-gated\ntransmit, independent of the CA helm-gate work).\n\n**Setup**\n- Chartplotter powered on (wake-only; we drive all control from ROS).\n- `sound_speed_bridge` running (AML SVS) — the watchdog depends on\n  `/bizzy/sensors/sound_speed/sound_speed`.\n- Launch: `ros2 launch garmin_sidescan garmin_sidescan.launch.py iface_ip:=\u003cgabby Marine-Net IP\u003e`.\n\n**Acceptance checks**\n- [ ] Imagery decodes to recognizable sidescan over a real bottom (channel map\n      {0,1,2}); view `~/waterfall_port` / `~/waterfall_starboard` and the\n      `RawSonarImage` topics.\n- [ ] Transmit on/off from ROS (`~/set_transmit` service and the `status`\n      control) — verify the GCV actually starts/stops pinging.\n- [ ] Range command from ROS changes the swath.\n- [ ] **Sound-speed safety interlock**: with the boat in the water and pinging,\n      lift the transducer out (or otherwise drop sound speed) and confirm the\n      watchdog stops transmit within `sv_timeout` (~12 s); confirm auto-resume\n      when it's back in the water.\n- [ ] Operator control set (`~/state`) renders in CAMP (status / range / tvg /\n      interference). Note: tvg/interference are GCV-10-derived and **unverified\n      on the GCV-20** — check whether they do anything.\n\n**Data to capture (for follow-ups)**\n- A short capture of all traffic from the chartplotter (`172.16.6.64`) over a\n  real bottom, to check whether it broadcasts a **depth** value we can receive\n  headlessly (Roland recalls ~0.3 m on the display) — feeds\n  rolker/marine_tools#16.\n- Note any decode glitches (the `dark_layer` signature-search limitation) for\n  the layer-length parsing follow-up.\n\nFindings should go back to rolker/marine_tools#15 / PR #17.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1780871014,"nonce":"/giSJYnGV/PVodLmWBcLGWGGTdk=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABFNIXqA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/228#issuecomment-4644280232"},"message":"## Post-hoc bag analysis (Run B, `2026-06-05T17-31-10Z`, ~99 min on water)\n\nThe two test runs after this issue opened didn't get full deployment logs, but the rqt-plugin\nbags are rich enough to answer several checkboxes here. Run A (`T15-22-20Z`) was the boat on\nthe pier — excluded. Analysis + scripts in `~/data/logs/analysis/2026-06-07_issue228/`.\n\n### Goal 3 (yaw-accel finding) — already RESOLVED in-repo; only the snap-roll watch is live\nMeasured realized yaw accel on `cmd_vel_smoothed`: `|d(yaw)/dt|` tops out at **exactly 3.00 rad/s²**\n(p99 = 0.97), i.e. the smoother is enforcing `nav2_params.240.yaml max_accel.z = 3.0`.\n\nThis is **not** a regression, and there is **no stale test**. The issue's premise (\"the #36 intent\nand `test_param_compose` are 0.5\") was already outdated when this was written: 3.0 was a deliberate\nfield tune (`d35a795`, 2026-06-02) — ±0.5 (~2 s ramp) lagged the CrabbingPathFollower PID →\nline-following hunting; **±3.0 (~0.3 s) restored clean tracking (cross-track 0.94 → 0.45 m),\nconfirmed on water** — and `test_param_compose` was **re-locked at ±3.0** in `737b2ce` (#45).\nBoth YAML and test agree at 3.0. ✅ Nothing to fix here; **close this Goal-3 box** as resolved.\n\nThe real residual is the *opposite* risk flagged in that commit: ±3.0 re-opens the deployment-197\nsnap-roll that ±0.5 guarded against. **Checked it in-bag** (SBG INS roll + gyro vs cmd yaw,\n`snap_roll_check.py`): the risk is real but sub-197. 10 sharp yaw-rate reversals (8 under GUIDED),\ninducing hull-roll excursions of **median 13°, p90 ~22°, max 22.1°** (corr with swing magnitude\n0.48), clustered in the GUIDED survey window t≈3350–3725 s — approaching, but not reaching, the\n~30° deployment-197 event. → Recommendation: **don't revert to 0.5** (too slow, confirmed);\nevaluate the **±1.5** compromise and/or sim-validate the roll response (any change updates both\nthe YAML and the #45 test lock together). Caveat: the 2.5 s excursion window can include sea-state\nroll; N=10.\n\n### Goal 1 (CA safety helm gate) — mechanism validated on water, with caveats\nThe gate fired live (state counts ~2 Hz: NONE 7725 / STOP 3895 / SLOWDOWN 228). Comparing\ngate input (`cmd_vel_smoothed`) vs output (`piloting_mode/autonomous/cmd_vel`), keyed by\n`collision_monitor_state`:\n\n- [x] **Nominal passthrough** — median in/out diff = 0.000 (linear \u0026 yaw) when idle.\n- [x] **Slowdown preserves yaw (anti-deadlock)** — 52/56 moving slowdown phases kept yaw\n      (median ratio 1.0): linear throttled to ~0.1 while yaw passes through up to ±1.0.\n- [x] **Reverse-assisted stop** — reverse thrust in the stop box, **clamped −0.5 m/s**; boat\n      decelerated (e.g. 0.44→0.03 m/s, 0.37→0.01 m/s).\n- [x] **Yaw-passthrough path left OFF** — in all **350** samples of STOP+reverse, `|yaw| = 0.000`.\n      `cancel_yaw_during_reverse=true` is honored on water.\n- [~] **Sole helm publisher** — no `ca_safety`/double-publish WARN in the (partly readable)\n      rosout; not a full node-graph confirmation.\n\n**Caveats:**\n- Most STOP-state time (1780 s of 1900 s) was the boat ~stationary — dominated by one 29-min\n  episode that was in **MANUAL** mode (parked with the pier in the stop box), i.e. **not** an\n  autonomous deadlock. Genuine *autonomous* (GUIDED) interventions are the t≈2894–3772 s window,\n  all at ≤~1.5 m/s.\n- **Still open:** no clean *high-speed, autonomous* survey-line obstacle encounter is in this\n  bag. The mechanism is proven; a dedicated autonomous obstacle pass at survey speed is needed\n  to close Goal 1.\n\n### Not answerable from these ROS bags\n- **M3 pings / QINSy export** — external to ROS (no M3 topic; DeltaT topic = 0, as expected).\n- **CAMP viz fills**, **`use_ca_safety:=false` fallback drill**, **OTH range**, **QINSy offload** —\n  operator-side / config / logistics, not in the bag.\n- Sensors confirmed healthy in-bag: SBG nav (`sbg/ekf_nav`), AML SVS (`sound_speed`), mavros GPS/odom.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}